So I would invite you, if you're watching this, to reflect on what behaviours crop up for you when you feel safe. Are they always adaptive, which would be leaning in, taking those breaths, enjoying those moments, or do they sometimes look a little bit different? What happens when we're not feeling safe is that we will likely strive all the harder. We might overwork, we might outperform people or want to, we might mask our true feelings, we might push people away, we might people please, or we might just generally feel like we are burning out or that we're not truly being seen for who we are. None of that feels very gratifying.
